GitHub Local HTML Preview handles the URL and HTML source of a GitHub file only after the user requests a preview. This information is processed locally solely to provide the preview. The extension developer does not collect, receive, retain, sell, or use it for advertising or profiling.

The selected HTML source is held briefly in Chrome's memory-backed session storage while the preview tab opens. It is deleted immediately after one read and is never persisted or synchronized.

When the user explicitly enables Allow active content, scripts and HTTPS assets referenced by the selected HTML may be downloaded from and communicate with third-party servers selected by that HTML. Path-relative assets are resolved against GitHub Raw URLs. This mode is disabled by default and runs inside an isolated sandbox.

Chrome separately asks before granting optional access to raw.githubusercontent.com. After approval, the extension corrects the declared response type of GitHub Raw stylesheets and scripts only in opted-in preview tabs. It does not read those response bodies, add credentials, remove browser MIME protections, or apply the rules to other tabs. The optional host approval persists in Chrome, while the tab-scoped rules are removed when active content is disabled or the preview tab closes.

Website content is used only for previews and is never sold, used for advertising, or read by the developer.
